From: OpenDesk <opendesk@openharmony.org>
Date: Tue, 25 Mar 2026 01:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/22] Lib/venv: HarmonyOS symlink fallback

On HarmonyOS, HMDFS (the user home filesystem) does not support
symlinks at all - os.symlink() always raises PermissionError due to
SELinux + Hmmac policies. This causes venv creation to fail at
the "create lib64 symlink" step (Issue #21197).

Solution: wrap os.symlink() in try/except and fall back to
os.makedirs() when symlink fails. This works because on HarmonyOS
platlibdir is 'lib' (not 'lib64'), so sysconfig.get_path() resolves
all paths under lib/ and never reads lib64/. The symlink is purely
defensive and never traversed on this platform.

Files modified:
  Lib/venv/__init__.py
---
diff --git a/Lib/venv/__init__.py b/Lib/venv/__init__.py
--- a/Lib/venv/__init__.py
+++ b/Lib/venv/__init__.py
@@ -137,7 +137,16 @@
             (sys.platform != 'darwin')):
             link_path = os.path.join(env_dir, 'lib64')
             if not os.path.exists(link_path):   # Issue #21643
-                os.symlink('lib', link_path)
+                try:
+                    os.symlink('lib', link_path)
+                except OSError:
+                    # HarmonyOS: HMDFS does not support symlinks (SELinux + Hmmac).
+                    # Fall back to creating lib64 as a real directory.
+                    # This works because Python's sysconfig.get_path() uses
+                    # sys.prefix (dynamic) rather than the static LIBDIR, so
+                    # pip/ensurepip install to lib/pythonX.Y/site-packages
+                    # regardless of whether lib64 is a symlink or directory.
+                    os.makedirs(link_path, exist_ok=True)
         context.bin_path = binpath = os.path.join(env_dir, binname)
         context.bin_name = binname
         context.env_exe = os.path.join(binpath, exename)
